  "description": "ORUZIN crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C104 H84 Er4 N12 O22,C2 H3 N1. From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.516-3.791 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.05-110.92°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C106H87N13O22Er4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
